For the normalized solution of \eqref{eq:A},
\begin{equation}
 A^2-x^2-2x^3\in9\Z[[x]].
\end{equation}
Consequently $9\mid\coef{n}{A^2}$ for every $n>3$,
as conjectured in A389474, FORMULA (3).

For every $k\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 A(x)^{3k}\equiv A(x^3)^k\pmod3.
\end{equation}
The normalized solution $B$ of \eqref{eq:B} satisfies
\begin{equation}
 B(x)^3\equiv B(x^3),\qquad
 B(x)^2\equiv x^2+2B(x^3)\pmod3.
\end{equation}
These prove A389474, FORMULA (4), and A389475,
FORMULA (4.a), (4.b).
